AB  - In this study, the co-culture of <i>Nigrospora oryzae</i> and <i>Beauveria bassiana</i>, the endophytes in the seeds of <i>Dendrobium officinale</i>, were examined for metabolite diversity. Five new azaphilones were isolated, and their structures were determined by spectral analysis. In terms of azaphilones, compound <b>2</b> had an unprecedented skeleton, with a bicyclic oxygen bridge. The antifungal selectivities of the metabolite produced by <i>N. oryzae</i> against its co-culture fungus, <i>B. bassiana</i>, and common pathogens exhibited competitive interaction in this mix-culture. Compounds <b>1</b> and <b>2</b> showed obvious nitric oxide (NO) inhibitory activity with ratios of 37%, and 39%, respectively, at a concentration of 50 μM.
